3. Systematic review methodology
The review used a PRISMA-guided search and screening process to identify relevant evidence and a structured methodological appraisal to support critical synthesis. Fig. 5 provides bibliometric context rather than an eligibility count: indexed publications increased markedly after 2020, while the 2026 value represents a partial-year observation and should not be interpreted as a decline. Publication volume demonstrates activity in the field but does not establish evidence quality or clinical readiness.
